<title>HONG KONG: Sui Chong interim net loss HK$14.76 mln.</title>
<headline>Sui Chong interim net loss HK$14.76 mln.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended June 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   6.80 loss  vs 2.69 gain</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    nil	  vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  29.89 loss vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    14.76 loss vs 4.97 profit</p>
<p>    Turnover		     335.02     vs 90.66</p>
<p>    Company name		 Sui Chong Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  N/A</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Construction and property concern Sui Chong, a subsidiary of Winfoong Investment Ltd, is the successor company of MKI Corp after a rescue plan.</p>
<p>Sui Chong shares were listed on October 12, 1995, by way of introduction.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional loss on the excess of revaluation deficit of investment properties over the available balance in the investment property revaluation reserve.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
